# db/

Readable, application-owned Goose SQL migrations live under
`migrations/NNNNN_snake_case.sql` with a zero-padded sequential prefix.
`embed.gen.go` embeds only `*.sql` files in the application binary and
exposes a filesystem rooted at that directory. Sequential prefixes rather
than timestamps keep generation byte-identical on every machine.

`00001_baseline.sql` is intentionally schema-neutral. Goose's provider
requires at least one source, and the baseline establishes version history
without inventing domain tables or extensions. Add application schema in
later migrations.

The migrator lives in `internal/platform/database/`; server startup never
applies migrations implicitly. Treat applied files as immutable and normally
recover with a new forward migration. Down sections remain useful for
disposable-database tests and deliberate operator recovery.

Run `nise db status` for a read-only history check and `nise db migrate` to
apply pending files under PostgreSQL advisory locking. There is no generated
`db down` command; production fixes are forward migrations by default.
